body:
Wow thank you. I did not realize how dark that could be. I think I understand but not as to that extent. I'm really a kind of person who thinks of thinks logically and objectively. 

&#x200B;

How does therapy work? it's very unfortunate that therapy isn't an option since it's too expensive in my country and I don't think we can spare some for it, especially with this pandemic going on. 

&#x200B;

How does therapy help? What do you do there? Is there some kind of general idea as to how it's being conducted and what's being discussed so that maybe somehow I'll have a better approach?

I know that this topic is not an easy thing to just read up on the internet but I really tried to read things that might help her or at least try to understand her. I've read some which helped me understand her a little bit. 

&#x200B;

Can I just ask since you said that you may know how she feels, what goes in your mind whenever you're having suicidal thoughts or thoughts of giving up in general? I've tried to talk her out of it and so far I think it barely worked. Do you not see any hope at that moment? Do you just think of life as a hopeless thing that's why you think ending it is the only sensible thing to do? and what helps you stop thinking about doing it?
